# PyScript's offline mode resolves its interpreters as ./pyscript/<name>/… relative to the
# page, so every directory that loads PyScript must answer that path with the one bundle at
# /pyscript/. tools/serve.py does this for ANY path locally, but Pages needs one line per
# directory (a splat may only end a pattern) — add a line when you add a page. A 200 is a
# rewrite, not a redirect.
/examples/:name/pyscript/* /pyscript/:splat 200
/playground/pyscript/* /pyscript/:splat 200
